# ============================================================
# COMBINED 6000 FORM + DIG PACKET + MAP READER
# ============================================================
#
# ONE standalone file. It does not import or call any other script.
#
# FLOW
#   1. Find the newest PDF in Downloads starting with "6000".
#   2. Read the 6000 form:
#        - main fields (Project Number, Wheel Count, MAOP, ...)
#        - Additional Notes for every section
#        - defect sections C-G (open/closed, anomalies, Dent/Gouge columns)
#   3. Use the Wheel Count to find the matching Dig Packet PDF.
#   4. ONLY if a Dig Packet exists, load the OCR models and read:
#        - Latitude / Longitude (multiple coordinates per row supported)
#        - handwritten Notes (character-first OCR + English correction)
#        - full-page map / alignment sheets (yellow note boxes and
#          pipeline data blocks)
#   5. One verification window shows everything. Every value has a
#      correction box; leave it blank to keep Python's value.
#      "Finish" prints the final values to the terminal (window stays open).
#
# ============================================================

